# fixedbugs, defect 063, 2026-09-19 (found by panel 165's spec-warden and
# ffi-pragmatist while pricing route 6; the write half by that sitting's
# completeness critic; closed by panel 166's route C in its C-emitted form).
#
# SYMPTOM: `sl_fill(p: s.name.ptr(), n: 64)` on an `i8[8]` field moved the
# sibling `id` from 7 to 1094795585 — `0x41414141` — at exit 0 with every suite
# green, and `sum_n(p: t.name.ptr(), n: 4096)` summed 4096 bytes of the stack at
# exit 0. Under `--sanitize`, `AddressSanitizer: stack-buffer-overflow`. Every
# overshoot from 9 to 4096 bytes was as silent: nothing trapped.
#
# CAUSE: the lend hands C the field's address and the CALL states the extent,
# and nothing related the number to the field — `sl_fill(p: ptr, n: i64)` is
# two independent parameters, so there was no *extent argument* to check. The
# first entry of the defect said one would be, and was corrected as
# unimplementable the day it was written.
#
# FIX: the relation is DECLARED, `p: ptr counted_by n`, and where the call
# states the extent as a compile-time constant the emitter writes one C
# assertion before the call — `_Static_assert((int64_t)(INT64_C(64)) <=
# (int64_t)sizeof(h0_s.name), …)` — so the number compared is C's own `sizeof`
# of the field, against the real header. `emit/ffi_extent.hero` reads the
# failure into `field_lend_extent`, on the number the author wrote, with the
# field's length as a `guess` fix. The `partial` record below is the shape a
# Heroes-side check could not judge, because its size is C's; `sizeof` of the
# field is right there too. The honest call beside each is in
# `tests/golden/run/ffi-a-lent-field-counted-by-a-constant.hero`.
extern "ffi-a-lent-field-extent-overstated.h"
    record Sl
        name: u8[8]
        id: i64
    record Both partial
        name: u8[8]
    function sl_make() -> Sl
    function both_make() -> Both
    function sl_fill(p: ptr counted_by n lent, n: i64)
    function sum_n(p: ptr counted_by n lent, n: i64) -> i64

function main()
    s: Sl @ sl_make()
    sl_fill(p: s.name.ptr(), n: 64)  #~ field_lend_extent
    print(s.id)
    t = sl_make()
    print(sum_n(p: t.name.ptr(), n: 4096))  #~ field_lend_extent
    b = both_make()
    print(sum_n(p: b.name.ptr(), n: 24))  #~ field_lend_extent
